{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who sets a mouth for man.</b> When I create man, I am the one who sets for him mouth and tongue — all the more so that I have the power to correct the heaviness of your mouth and the heaviness of your tongue to speak fluently." "<b>Mute.</b> Corresponding to 'who sets a mouth.' Deaf — Scripture placed it between deaf and blind because it applies to both of them, as it is said (Isaiah 42:20) 'פקוח אזנים ולא ישמע' (open-eared yet does not hear), (Isaiah 42:7) 'לפקוח עינים עורות' (to open blind eyes)." "<b>Or blind.</b> Rashi explained: who made them blind when you fled, and they did not see. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory: for it is written above 'וישמע פרעה' — Rashi explained: he handed him over to the executioner to kill him, and the sword did not prevail against him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Reading חרש (deaf) in the lemma as the subject; the Hebrew text is slightly compressed and the word פקח (deaf) in the lemma may be a variant spelling of חרש, here resolved contextually."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:09.315533256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}